  "observations": [
    "The previous one-degree restriction ignored positive explicit angles below one degree. Polygon selection, region matching and smooth-candidate tangent classification now use one effective angle. Omitted and zero angles preserve the default.",
    "The 0.002-radian intrinsic boundary is supported by measured positive-angle holdouts. An initial interpretation using the OpenNURBS 0.1-degree minimum was disproved by near-boundary native cases and removed before qualification.",
    "The exact 0.002-radian case changes native branch with model scale. The existing conservative angular roundoff margin declines that edge, including one native seven-control output. No exact-boundary parity is claimed.",
    "Polynomial and positive rational clocks retain certified directed straight-region images. Unequal regions, line companions and a spatial frame require the same angle when constructing their common knot chart.",
    "Coarse initial cubics can smooth larger corners suppressed by the requested angle when the existing complete half-tolerance certificate succeeds. Resolved corners cannot be erased by the smooth fallback.",
    "Rounded degree elevation can produce slightly curved spans that exact straight-region extraction declines. Suppressed/adaptive fits remain explicit limitations. No fitting-distance acceptance policy was relaxed."
  ],
